<PageTitle>Terms of Use - Catkoom</PageTitle>

<LegalPage Title="Terms of Use" Updated="October 17, 2026">
    <p>
        These terms explain the rules for using Catkoom, a place to read and publish webcomics. By creating an
        account or using the site, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use Catkoom.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Who can use Catkoom</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>You must be at least 13 years old to create an account.</li>
        <li>You must give your real date of birth. We use it to decide which series you can see (see section 5). Giving a false date of birth breaks these terms and can lead to your account being removed.</li>
        <li>If you're old enough to hold an account but not yet an adult where you live, make sure a parent or guardian is okay with you using the site.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Your account</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Keep your password and sign-in methods (including any Google or Facebook account you use to sign in) secure. You're responsible for what happens under your account.</li>
        <li>Pick a username that isn't misleading and doesn't pretend to be another person or organization.</li>
        <li>Tell us if you think someone else has accessed your account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. Content you post</h2>
    <p>
        "Content" means anything you upload or write on Catkoom: series, chapters, cover images, creator posts,
        comments, replies, profile details and reports.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>You own your content.</strong> We don't take ownership of it.</li>
        <li><strong>You give us permission to show it.</strong> By posting, you let Catkoom store, display and distribute your content on the site so the service can work. This permission lasts as long as the content is on Catkoom and ends when you delete it, apart from copies that remain in backups for a limited time.</li>
        <li><strong>You must have the right to post it.</strong> Only upload work you made yourself or have clear permission to use. Don't post other people's comics, artwork or writing without permission.</li>
        <li><strong>Co-authors.</strong> If you add co-authors to a series, they can edit it. Only add people you trust.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. What isn't allowed</h2>
    <p>You may not post or do any of the following on Catkoom:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Anything illegal, or anything that sexualizes or endangers children.</li>
        <li>Harassment, threats, or hate speech aimed at people because of who they are.</li>
        <li>Spam, scams, or misleading promotion.</li>
        <li>Content that infringes someone else's copyright or other rights.</li>
        <li>Malware, or attempts to break, overload or get around the security of the site, including its age restrictions.</li>
        <li>Creating accounts to avoid a ban or restriction.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Age ratings and mature content</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Every series has an age rating: 13+, 16+ or 18+. Creators choose the rating when they create or edit a series.</li>
        <li>As a creator, you must choose a rating that fits your series. If you're not sure, choose the higher one. We may change a series' rating, or remove the series, if the rating is wrong.</li>
        <li>Readers only see series that fit the age on their account. A series rated above your age is hidden from you.</li>
        <li>Age checks rely on the date of birth you give us. They're a tool to help keep younger readers away from mature content, but they aren't perfect.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. Reports and moderation</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Anyone with an account can report a series, creator, post or comment. Reports ask for a category and a written reason, so please explain the problem honestly and don't file false reports.</li>
        <li>We may remove content, limit features, suspend or ban accounts that break these terms. We'll use our judgment and don't have to give advance notice, though we'll try to be fair.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>7. Payments and creator earnings</h2>
    <p>
        Creators may be able to connect a Stripe account to receive payments. Payments are handled by Stripe, and
        using Stripe means accepting Stripe's own terms. How earnings are calculated and shared will be explained
        here once those features launch: [revenue share and payout terms to be added before launch].
    </p>

    <h2>8. Copyright complaints</h2>
    <p>
        If you think content on Catkoom copies your work without permission, send us the details at
        [contact email]. Include a link to the content, what work it copies, and how we can reach you.
        We'll review it and may remove the content while we do.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Sign-in with other services</h2>
    <p>
        You can sign in with Google or Facebook. If you do, those services have their own terms and privacy
        policies, and we only receive the information described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>10. No guarantees</h2>
    <p>
        Catkoom is provided "as is". We try to keep it running and safe, but we can't promise it will always be
        available or error-free, and we aren't responsible for content posted by users. To the extent the law
        allows, we aren't liable for indirect or consequential losses from using the site.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Ending your account</h2>
    <p>
        You can delete your account at any time from your account settings. We can suspend or close accounts that
        break these terms. Sections that need to survive an account closing (such as those about content
        permissions, copyright and limits on liability) continue to apply afterwards.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. When we make an important change, we'll tell you on the site
        or by email. Using Catkoom after a change means you accept the new terms.
    </p>

